        "content": "<p>While reviewing the graph API, I noticed that the proof of</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Connected</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induce_compl_singleton_of_degree_eq_one</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>can be shortened using</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Preconnected</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induce_of_degree_eq_one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">ᶜ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The unique neighbor handles nonemptiness. This would remove the duplicate proof and move the lemma from <code>Acyclic</code> to <code>Connectivity.Connected</code>. No API changes required, and the lemma can be imported without <code>Acyclic</code>.</p>",
